canlin_ev_op_complete(ev, h, status, void *payload, bytes, release) carries an untyped payload. src/module/module.c map_op casts d->payload to const canlin_module_result * with no type tag, so a second producer with a different payload shape would be read wrongly. Latent today: the only producer is src/llm/llm.c:897, which passes the correct type, and include/canlin/module.h:67 documents the contract in prose only. Done when the payload carries a type tag or a typed wrapper exists. Found by the 2026-11-14 review.

Implementation in the runtime lane: canlin_module_result now begins with an ASCII-magic type tag (CANLIN_MODULE_RESULT_TAG 0x4d524553u, 'MRES', like the existing source tags); src/module/module.c map_op checks the tag (and that the payload is at least sizeof(canlin_module_result)) before reading a single field of the body, and refuses an unstamped payload with ok=false code=unavailable instead of following foreign pointers. The ev scheduler stays payload-agnostic: canlin_ev_op_complete's signature is unchanged. Test: t/module/test_module.c test_op_payload_shape (a second producer's payload of another shape, full size and truncated) - red without the check (the foreign producer's own code 'denied' reached Lua), green with it; registered in main(). Existing constructions in that file now carry the tag.

Neighbour lane: src/llm/llm.c needed the producer-side stamp (one line, res->r.tag = CANLIN_MODULE_RESULT_TAG, in req_pump). Without it every llm result would be refused, so the one-line edit was made and is reported here for the netllm lane to confirm. Without it the module layer refuses every llm result and the assistant's results break.

Drift found, not fixed here (other lanes): (1) src/app/assistant.c:369 route_done reads d->payload as const canlin_module_result * without checking the tag - the same hole in the platform lane; (2) core API spec 6 records 'canlin_module_result {value | code, message}' - now stale, the doc lane owns it; (3) the llm->module op-completion path (src/llm/llm.c:897) has no test at all - t/app/test_assistant.c does not drive an OP delivery.

